1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A place to ask questions. A place to make discoveries.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Welcome to the learning lab.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Instructor: “Good morning, everyone. Let’s look inside a computer.”

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
“By the end of today, you’ll know how the main components work together.”

5
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:40,000
“The motherboard connects all the components.”

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
“The CPU executes instructions. RAM holds the work in progress.”

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,500
“Storage keeps your files, even when the power is off.”

8
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:53,000
“The graphics card processes images and sends them to the display.”

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Student: “Why do we need both RAM and storage?”

10
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,500
Instructor: “Think of RAM as your desk. It holds what you’re working on.”

11
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:11,000
“Storage is your bookshelf. It keeps things until you need them.”

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,000
“Your turn: match each computer component to its job.”

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
“Good thinking. The processor works with the data held in RAM.”

14
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,000
“Now save your work. It will be there next time.”

15
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,000
An idea becomes a keystroke. A keystroke becomes understanding.

16
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Small details. Real progress.

17
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,000
“Connect, process, remember, store, and display. Every part has a purpose.”

18
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:01,000
“Keep asking questions. That’s how every discovery begins.”

19
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Bright minds. A brighter tomorrow.
